cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PlantaCRISPAI in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PlantaCRISPAI: An AI-powered universal CRISPR genotyping platform for Sanger sequencing data from genome-edited plants"
abstract: >-
  PlantaCRISPAI is a browser-based platform that genotypes CRISPR-edited plants
  directly from Sanger sequencing data. It parses Applied Biosystems .ab1 files
  natively, aligns reads to a reference amplicon with a gap-aware Smith-Waterman
  algorithm, localises the Cas9 cut site from the guide RNA, and classifies each
  plant as wild-type, mosaic, heterozygous or homozygous using a generation-aware
  ensemble of rule-based, ICE-equivalent and Random Forest scores. It also
  designs CAPS and dCAPS markers for PCR-based screening and scores candidate
  guide RNAs for efficiency and CAPS compatibility. All computation runs
  client-side; no sequence data leaves the user's browser.
